  "observations": "Short-pad chromatography\nFritted funnel (x mL, por. 4), suction adapter, 250 mL RBF, T-connector, diaphragm pump\nAdd 30 g of neutral alumina\nAdd THF to fully wet the alumina\nAdd the reaction mixture\nElute with suction and THF until the eluate becomes pale red → 220 mL, alumina pad blue-green at the top, pale red at the bottom\nStore in the fridge o/n\nRotovap\nDry under vacuum Schlenk line, 1 h\n\nRT 21.9 °C, RH 32 %\nCHCl₃ deacidification\n250 mL RBF\nAdd basic alumina 40 g\nAdd CHCl₃ 150 mL and swirl\nFritted funnel (x mL, por. 4), suction adapter, 250 mL RBF, diaphragm pump\nFilter the mixture under suction\n\nReprecipitation\nAdd 50 mL of purified CHCl₃ to the flask and sonicate → dark red solution\nAdd 280 mL of n-heptane, swirl, sonicate\nStore in fridge (0 °C) for 1 h 20 min\nFritted funnel (x mL, por. 4), suction adapter, 250 mL RBF, diaphragm pump [fritted funnel could be smaller]\nFilter the mixture under suction → dark brown filtrate\nFilter the filtrate again → faint brown filtrate\nTransfer & rinse w/ 2 x (12 mL of purified CHCl₃ + 40 mL of heptane)\nRinse with 2 × 30 mL of petroleum ether\nDry under vacuum (desiccator, diaphragm pump, 4 days) → reddish brown solid\n\nAnalysis\nRT 21.8 °C, RH 39%\n20 mL vial with PTFE sealing (tare: 15.29431 g)\nWeigh\n→ 1H NMR P (CDCl₃, DMSO; U1.834; N PROTON 20 ppm; O1P 6, SW 22) (dark red solution)\nStore in the fridge"
